load @term/seed/type/self
  find self-type

# The booleans, the simplest inductive type, encoded as a self type whose body is its own eliminator. This is the
# template every inductive type follows: a self type carrying its induction principle, two introductions (true and
# false), and a dependent eliminator that uses a boolean by giving a result for each value. The naturals and everything
# after follow the same shape.
#
# The rules. Introduction: true and false both inhabit the boolean. Elimination: to use a boolean, give a result for
# the true case and a result for the false case; the eliminator selects one. Computation: eliminating true yields the
# true-case result, eliminating false yields the false-case result.
form boolean
  link encoding, like self-type
